I'd say it's more like "If you know what you need, and what you need
isn't a permanent light source, and you've blessed the lamp and fixed
your luck, then by all means go for it.  If you have no pressing
needs, or if you don't really know what you might need, save it."

That still has some major caveats, though.  If you don't expect to
survive long enough to make good use of the lamp as a ligh source,
then by all means spend the early wish on DSM -- it'll at least
improve your survival odds a bit.  Which I suppose is what you're
saying above.

I guess one could try to make some sort of a decision tree for it:

1. Is the lamp blessed?  If not, wait until you can bless it.

2. Is your luck positive?  If not, fix that first!

3. Are you planning to bless and quaff some smoky potions?  If yes,
   you may want to do that first to maximize your odds.  (If you don't
   understand this question, ignore it.)

4. Have you done Sokoban yet?  If not, do you expect to make it that
   far?  If yes, consider trying to get reflection from there first.

5. Do you have another one?  If yes, just use this one for the wish.

6. Have you ever reached the Sanctum before?  If yes, are you planning
   on getting there quickly?  If yes, you probably have little use for
   a permanent light source, so just use the wish.

7. Have you done the Castle?  If not, do you expect to make it there?
   If not, can you think of an item that would help you get that far
   more than the magic lamp will?  If yes, wish for it.

At this point, you either have a character who's done the Castle or
expects to make it there, and is not an experienced player going for a
fast ascension, or you have a pre-Castle character who doesn't know
what to wish for or just wants the light source.  In either case, my
advice at this point would be to keep the lamp for now, unless and
until you find yourself needing a specific item more than you need the
light source and the possibility of a future wish.

Okay, it's a pretty silly checklist, and probably omits a lot of
cases.  It also says little about what to wish for, although we do
have the wishing spoiler for that.

There's a hidden assumption in Q4 that you'll want a reflection source
(SDSM) if you don't find one in Sokoban.  This may be oversimplified;
some people may try to get it from Medusa's instead (but that's a long
way to go without reflection, and you'll have to fight Medusa herself
the hard way) while others may just go for GDSM regardless.  In any
case, it's a special case of a more general rule: if you expect to
make it to a place where you have a reasonable chance of finding an
item you might otherwise have wished for, then it may pay to save that
wish until later.

